resources.string:
① Tap "Open Preview" and grant camera permission on first use (cascade models are copied on first launch, please wait a moment);
② A red box appears and tracks the face in real time; frontal, left and right profile faces (multi-cascade fusion) are all detectable, evenly lit scenes work best;
③ Tap "Switch Camera" to toggle front/back; tracking resets and re-detects after switching;
④ Tap "Close Preview" or go back to the main screen to release the camera;
⑤ Note: frontal faces are detected by a union of two models and profile faces by a dedicated model; heavy occlusion or long distances may still cause misses.

This feature is based on the "search video with current frame" retrieval flow of the video recognition module, turning offline retrieval into real-time camera tracking:
① Target acquisition (box-select = the retrieval "query"): press and drag on the preview to box-select an object; on release, the next frame uses that ROI as the query target for template building — the same idea as capturing the current picture as the query frame in retrieval;
② Feature extraction (same feature space as video retrieval, Ch. 10): color feature is a 64-bin luma histogram (L1 normalized); texture feature is a Sobel gradient-orientation histogram (18 bins, magnitude-weighted, significant edges only, orientations folded to [0°,180°)); an HSV hue histogram (32 bins, low-saturation/low-value pixels masked) is also extracted for CamShift backprojection;
③ Candidate generation (CamShift, continuously adaptive mean shift): the template hue histogram backprojects the whole frame into a probability map, and CamShift iterates to the probability-density peak near the previous window, adapting to target position and size changes;
④ Comprehensive-similarity verification (the retrieval metric): Sim = 0.6·histogram intersection (color) + 0.4·cosine (texture) ∈ [0,1], exactly the same as the keyframe retrieval metric — a passing similarity confirms the same target and shows the green box with live similarity; 15 consecutive frames below 0.35 declare the target lost;
⑤ Adaptive template: when tracking is stable (similarity > 0.8), every 5 frames the current target features are blended in with a 0.2 weight, adapting to gradual lighting and pose changes;
⑥ Data pipeline: camera NV21 frame → RGBA → orientation correction (front camera mirrored) → grayscale/HSV → CamShift tracking + feature verification → green box and similarity drawing → ANativeWindow rendering, all on the preview callback thread for real-time performance.

① Tap "Open Preview" and grant camera permission on first use;
② Press and drag on the preview to box-select the object to track (objects with rich color and texture such as books, cups or phones work best); tracking starts immediately on release;
③ The green box follows the target in real time, with the comprehensive similarity shown above the picture and in the right panel;
④ If the target leaves the frame or is occluded, a loss is reported — box-select again to resume; tap "Re-select" to change the tracked target at any time;
⑤ After "Switch Camera" the target must be box-selected again; tap "Close Preview" or go back to release the camera;
⑥ Note: plain-colored, reflective or texture-poor targets have weak discriminative features and are easy to lose; evenly lit scenes with feature-rich targets work best.
